{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"The symbol gap is already zero: both libraries export the same 384 `png_*` symbols. The Rust crate achieves this by compiling the complete C source set into a renamed object and exposing Rust ABI trampolines, so I’m treating the FFI wrappers—not direct Rust calls—as the verification target. I’m generating the mandatory mechanical inventories before adding tests."}}
